# Personal settings for the development environment.
# Copy this file to .env.local at the repository root and uncomment what you need.
# tools/dev/activate.ps1, tools/dev/activate.sh, and .envrc load .env.local; Git ignores it.
#
# One KEY=VALUE per line. A line starting with # is a comment, and quotes around a value are
# optional. The PowerShell script, the bash script, and direnv each parse this file their own
# way, so keep to what all three read alike:
#   - comments only on lines of their own;
#   - no $ and no backslash in a value: write paths with forward slashes;
#   - no empty value, which PowerShell treats as unsetting the variable: comment the line out;
#   - no line that is neither KEY=VALUE nor a comment: the scripts skip it with a warning, but
#     direnv may refuse the whole file;
#   - UTF-8 without a byte order mark.

# A Unity Editor executable for every compile and test run, instead of the version each
# project names in ProjectSettings/ProjectVersion.txt.
# UNITY_EDITOR=C:/Program Files/Unity/Hub/Editor/6000.6.7f1/Editor/Unity.exe

# The folder that holds one folder per installed Editor version, when Unity Hub installs
# Editors outside its default location.
# UNITY_HUB_EDITOR_ROOT=D:/Unity/Hub/Editor

# 1 runs the Steam backend's integration tests against the Steam client on this machine
# (Steam's test app 480; the client must be running and signed in).
# MU3LIBRARY_STEAM_TESTS=1
